  "result": "I fixed it. Subcommands now pick up their own section of `default_map`, and the full test suite still passes.\n\nA child context was inheriting the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own command name. So a map like `{\"sub\": {\"x\": \"mapped\"}}` was looked up for `x` at the top level and never matched. The fix is a one-line change in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py:392`. It now reads `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\nI checked it with a group and a `sub` command that has `--x`. Invoking `sub` with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"x\": \"mapped\"}}` now prints `mapped`. Before the fix it printed the option's own default.\n\nI didn't add a regression test for this one, or for the earlier fixes. I can add them if you want.",
